From 6179db59457bd24a823fc320eb03e92fdbcb436a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Huskins <ahuskins@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 02:00:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] codecs: v4l2 avc decoder: stop advertising adaptive-playback

On Raspberry Pi 4 the bcm2835-codec stateful decoder cannot change
resolution on a running queue. When the decoder advertises the
adaptive-playback feature, ExoPlayer/Media3 based apps (Disney+, Hulu,
Peacock) reuse the codec across adaptive-bitrate resolution switches.
The driver then rejects the format change:

  bcm2835-codec bcm2835-codec: vidioc_s_fmt queue busy

and the component fails with C2 error 0xe, which the apps surface as
"Decoder failed: c2.v4l2.avc.decoder" 15 s to a few minutes into
playback.

Without adaptive-playback, Media3 re-creates the decoder on resolution
changes and playback continues. Tested on rpi4 (Android 14, build
7104721dd81f) by bind-mounting the modified file over
/vendor/etc/media_codecs_v4l2_c2.xml and restarting the media service:
Disney+ plays through quality switches with no decoder errors.
---
 common/codecs/media_codecs_v4l2_c2.xml | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/common/codecs/media_codecs_v4l2_c2.xml b/common/codecs/media_codecs_v4l2_c2.xml
index e2ae7a0..f3cfc85 100644
--- a/common/codecs/media_codecs_v4l2_c2.xml
+++ b/common/codecs/media_codecs_v4l2_c2.xml
@@ -22,7 +22,6 @@
            <Limit name="bitrate" range="1-62500000" />
            <Limit name="concurrent-instances" max="8" />
            <Limit name="performance-point-3840x2160" range="30-30" />
-           <Feature name="adaptive-playback" />
        </MediaCodec>
     </Decoders>
 </MediaCodecs>
-- 
2.43.0

